      "text": "To find the greatest possible value of \\( x \\) that is a positive multiple of 3 and \\( x^3 < 1000 \\), we need to determine the cube root of 1000 and then find the largest integer multiple of 3 that is less than or equal to this cube root. Here are the steps:\n\n1. Calculate the cube root of 1000:\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt[3]{1000} = 10\n   \\]\n   This means \\( x^3 < 1000 \\) implies \\( x < 10 \\).\n\n2. Identify the largest integer that is a multiple of 3 and less than 10. The multiples of 3 are 3, 6, and 9.\n\n3. Determine the greatest of these multiples:\n   \\[\n   9\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the greatest possible value of \\( x \\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{9}\n\\]",
